2,1,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
3,1,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
4,1,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
5,1,1,talk,Kenji,,"Hi everyone! I'm excited to help. I think we should really check if the construction plans are realistic. I'm worried about delays once digging starts, so we need to know who can actually do the work.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"A prudent start, Kenji. While the ""who"" is important, I believe we must also consider the ""how"" the park actually functions. A beautiful blueprint is useless if it ignores the reality of the terrain and the people.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Minato,,I agree with Benjamin. I wonder who will take care of the park after it is finished? I want to know if there are enough people to keep it beautiful every day.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Minako,,"I agree with the need for realism. However, we should look at the actual longevity of previous projects. Blueprints often hide future decay, so I want to see how past works are holding up today.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree with all of you. To ensure the park remains a sanctuary without draining the city's coffers, I believe we must look closely at the actual long-term costs of upkeep and maintenance.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"That makes sense! To figure out the construction side, I'll look into the regional firms tendering for earth-moving and the depot phasing notes on hoarding the site. That should show us if the timeline is realistic.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,I shall complement your focus on logistics with a look at the ground truth. I'll examine the timed counts of weekday crossings and the drainage callouts and August heat readings to see how the site actually behaves.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Minato,,"I want to see who is helping now. I will look into the groundskeeping roll and bought-in services, and also the volunteer groups working with the division. I hope we find many kind people.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Minako,,"To assess the actual quality of the city's commissions, I will look into the condition of works from the earlier programme and the record of the eastern avenue planting. I want to see the results.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Jonathan,,I will examine the upkeep ledger spend per hectare and the terms of the regional habitat fund. It is vital to know if the funding is sustainable and what the actual costs are.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Kenji,,"I think we've covered all the bases! We have the construction, the usage, the staffing, the quality, and the money. I'm really curious to see what the earth-moving firms say about the site.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed, we have cast a wide net. I suspect the data on drainage and foot traffic will provide a sobering contrast to the optimism of the architectural renderings. I look forward to the revelations.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Minato,,I hope the people who work there are happy. It would be nice if the new plan makes it easier for everyone to help each other and keep the park a peaceful place.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Minako,,"It is important that we remain objective. Once we have the data, we can determine which plan is truly sustainable rather than just visually appealing. I look forward to seeing the actual state of previous works.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. Let us hope the data provides a clear path forward. I believe a realistic understanding of the financial burden will help us choose a plan that is truly sustainable for the city.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm ready! Let's see what we find out. I'll be cheering for a plan that actually gets finished on time! See you all in the next round!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Patience is a virtue, Kenji, though I share your anticipation. Let us hope the evidence speaks clearly so we aren't merely guessing at the park's future. I shall see you all in the next round.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Minato,,"I'm a little nervous, but I'm excited to learn more about the people who love the park. I hope we can find a plan that is kind to everyone. See you soon!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Minako,,"I am ready as well. Let us proceed to the findings. I will be looking for the truth in the results, not the promises in the plans. See you in the next round.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Jonathan,,I am also ready. I will reflect on the figures quietly and wait for our next meeting. I wish you all a peaceful interval before we reconvene. See you in the next round.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
