30,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Minato,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, I found some worrying stuff! Only two firms are willing to do the earth-moving, and they both warned about clay subsoil and slippage risks. That could really mess up our timeline if we aren't careful!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems the earth is as stubborn as the bureaucracy. My findings are equally sobering: the site is a heat trap, and the drainage is failing. Moreover, people are carving their own paths to the tram.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minato,,"I found out that there are only seven people on the groundskeeping roll now, which is much fewer than before. But I was happy to see that some kind volunteers are already helping out on weekends!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"My findings confirm a pattern of poor longevity. While some structural work holds, the surface finishes are failing, and half the eastern avenue trees died due to negligent aftercare contracts. We cannot trust the drawings alone.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The financial data is concerning. Planted areas cost triple to maintain compared to hard surfaces, yet two-thirds of our funding only covers planting. We risk creating a beautiful space that the city cannot afford to keep.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, that's scary! If the drainage is failing and there's clay slippage, the digging will be even harder. We need a plan that doesn't require too much deep digging or complex earth-moving.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely, Kenji. We must avoid any design that treats the park as a static painting. If we ignore the existing drainage failures and the natural desire of pedestrians to take the shortest route, we are merely designing a future ruin.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Jonathan, it sounds like the plants are very expensive to look after. Since there are so few groundskeepers left, I worry that the plants might get sad and die like the trees Minako mentioned.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, you are correct. The eastern avenue failure proves that planting without a guaranteed maintenance contract is a waste of resources. We must prioritize a plan with durable materials and realistic care requirements.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, your concern is well-founded. If we prioritize planting to secure the habitat fund, we may inadvertently create a financial burden that the current staffing levels simply cannot sustain. We must balance ecological goals with fiscal reality.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I agree! We should look for a plan that uses those durable materials Minako mentioned. If we keep the earth-moving simple, we can avoid those slippage risks and actually finish the project on time!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Logic dictates that we prioritize a design that accommodates the tram commuters' shortcuts rather than fighting them. A plan that ignores these ""desire lines"" will simply result in trampled greenery and wasted funds.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I think we should also look for a plan that the volunteers can help with. Since there are so few staff, maybe the kind people who already help can take care of the park together.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"That is a helpful suggestion, Minato. However, we must be careful not to rely solely on volunteers for critical care. We need a design that is fundamentally robust and easy to maintain.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree with Minako. While volunteers are a blessing, the city's budget must be the foundation. We should be wary of any plan that maximizes planting just to capture the habitat fund if it creates an unsustainable long-term deficit.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm on board! Let's find a plan that's simple to build, doesn't fight the soil, and is easy to keep up. I can't wait to see the candidates and pick the best one!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. Let us hope the candidates offer a pragmatic approach. A design that respects the heat, the water, and the pedestrians will be the only one that truly survives the first year. I am ready.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minato,,I hope the plans have a way to make the workers and volunteers feel happy and not too tired. I'm looking forward to seeing which one is the most gentle and sustainable for everyone.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,"I am also ready. We have a clear set of criteria now: structural durability, realistic maintenance, and a design that respects the site's physical constraints. I will vote for the plan that proves most resilient.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I am also ready. I will be looking for a balance that secures necessary funding without compromising the city's future financial stability. Let us evaluate the candidates with a clear eye for sustainability.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
